    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the entry point, especially at night.\n• Trim tree branches and shrubs along the access drive to maintain clearance for fire apparatus and ambulances along the full length of the driveway.\n• Clear vegetation from both sides of the access drive to widen the usable travel width for large emergency vehicles.\n• Designate and mark a turnaround area near the residence so arriving crews do not have to back out the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep the turnaround area free of parked vehicles, equipment, and stored materials at all times.\n• Thin dense vegetation between the access drive and the detached structure so responders can reach that building without navigating through heavy brush.\n• Post a visible property map or address placard near the driveway entrance showing the location of the main residence and the detached structure.\n• Keep the access drive surface clear of debris, fallen branches, and overgrowth that could slow or block emergency vehicle movement."
